Perfect! I can see the bug clearly. The function is trying to return `parts[1]` (the second element) when it should return `parts[0]` (the first element). This is a classic off-by-one error.

- For `'hello world'`, the split gives `['hello', 'world']`, and `parts[1]` returns `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- For `'solo'`, the split gives `['solo']`, and `parts[1]` causes an IndexError because there's no second element
