Perfect! I found and fixed the bug in src/parse.py:4. The issue was a classic off-by-one error where the function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused it to return 'world' instead of 'hello' and throw an IndexError for single-word inputs. All tests now pass.
